{"status":"completed","summary":"Hardened `/tmp` and `/dev/shm` on node1 with `noexec,nosuid,nodev`. Both are persistent tmpfs mounts, remain writable with mode 1777, and recovered correctly after reboot. CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were retained.","actions_performed":["Updated `/etc/fstab` with hardened tmpfs entries for `/tmp` and `/dev/shm`.","Applied the hardened mounts immediately.","Verified execution and device-node access are denied on both mounts.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified a changed boot identity.","Reverified configuration, mount options, permissions, writability, and enforced behavior after reboot."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Harden `/tmp` with noexec, nosuid, and nodev, persistently","command_ids":["cmd-5ca10851e9994262","cmd-34cd454265ce43a6","cmd-fbd792a5110f4a01"],"summary":"The fstab entry persists `nodev,nosuid,noexec`; `/proc/mounts` confirms all three active flags. Direct execution and device-node access are denied before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Harden `/dev/shm` with noexec, nosuid, and nodev, persistently","command_ids":["cmd-5ca10851e9994262","cmd-34cd454265ce43a6","cmd-fbd792a5110f4a01"],"summary":"The fstab entry persists `nodev,nosuid,noexec`; `/proc/mounts` confirms all three active flags. Direct execution and device-node access are denied before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-29bd27052cff4606","cmd-fbd792a5110f4a01"],"summary":"Post-restart evidence reports CentOS release 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5, matching the original kernel."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-dd32da5cb2f9413d","cmd-09c289eafd7f4ca0","cmd-2a8b6be465ad49bc","cmd-fbd792a5110f4a01"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was c7943ca1-7a2f-4b77-8000-000000000000; reboot was acknowledged; the new boot ID is d5c91caf-fd5b-4234-8000-000000000000; both hardened mounts and their behavior recovered successfully."}]}
